==French==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fr|frm|espaule}}, from {{inh|fr|fro|espalle}}, from {{inh|fr|VL.||*spatla}}<ref>https://books.google.com/books?id=SdsxAAAAMAAJ&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false</ref>, from {{inh|fr|LL.|spatula|spathula|flat, broad piece}}<ref>http://www.cnrtl.fr/etymologie/%C3%A9paule</ref>, diminutive of {{inh|fr|la|spatha||straight sword}} (whence French {{m|fr|épée||sword}}). {{doublet|fr|spatule}}, which was a borrowing.

